      say: `Learn's page on automatic assignment policies is the procedure. A policy carries a membership rule in the dynamic group syntax. Entitlement management creates assignments for users who match, removes them for users who stop matching, and a grace period can keep access for a while. Learn suggests one automatic policy per package, warns that overlap can lose users their access, caps a rule at fifteen thousand identities, and needs the Identity Governance Administrator. And from November third, 2026, a policy using member-of is quarantined: it stays, but does nothing.`,
      detail: `Learn's Configure an automatic assignment policy for an access package page is the procedure. A policy carries a membership rule in the dynamic group syntax; entitlement management creates assignments for users who match and removes them for users who stop matching; a grace period can keep access for a while after a user leaves scope. Learn suggests one automatic policy per package, and supports more only if no user ever matches two at once or moves from one to another, "otherwise users can lose access." It creates a hidden dynamic group per policy that nobody should modify or reuse, allows at most 15,000 identities in a policy's rule, and needs Identity Governance Administrator: catalog owners and access package managers can't create automatic policies. From November 3, 2026, a policy whose rule uses memberOf is quarantined: it stays, but adds and removes nothing until the operator is removed; Learn publishes a read-only script to find them.`,
