      say: `The lint has nine rules. Member-of in a rule is a finding. Two automatic policies on one package that a user matches at once is a finding, and two disjoint ones a warning. More than fifteen thousand identities is a finding. A rule with no coded slot or worker type warns, because a department name breaks on a rename. A policy must both create and remove. A grace over fourteen days warns. Requests need the manager and a fallback. And no privileged package may be assigned by rule.`,
      detail: `AA-01, Finding: a rule that uses memberOf (Learn: quarantined from November 3, 2026). AA-02, Finding; Warn: two automatic policies on one package that a user matches at once (Finding); two disjoint ones (Warn) (Learn). AA-03, Finding: more than 15,000 identities in scope (Learn). AA-04, Warn: a rule on no coded slot or worker type (design guidance, from Book 03, Chapter 10). AA-05, Finding: an automatic policy that doesn't both create and remove (design guidance; Learn's defaults). AA-06, Warn: a grace period over 14 days (design guidance, from Book 04, Chapter 09). AA-07, Finding: a request policy without the manager as approver and a fallback (Learn; the guide's step 5). AA-08, Warn: a rule outside the evaluator's subset (lint it with examples/dynamic-rules). AA-09, Finding: a tier T0, T1 or privileged package assigned by rule (the guide's step 7; SCuBA MS.AAD.7.5v1).`,
