      sources: "Sources: Chapter 04, “The mover's residual review”; “What it leaves to you.”",
      say: `The residual review takes the mover's old and new attributes, the effective date, their package assignments, their group memberships and the policy files. For each automatic assignment, it re-evaluates the rule on the new attributes: kept, or removed at the end of the grace. Anything from another policy is marked for review. Dynamic groups are rule-managed, groups a held package grants are package-managed, and anything else goes to review. The sheet goes to the manager of record, and the interval from transfer to review is measured.`,
      detail: `residual takes the mover (old and new attributes, the effective date, and the review's completion once it closes), the mover's access package assignments, their group memberships and the policy files. For each assignment, it re-evaluates the automatic policy's rule against the new attributes: kept by rule, or removed by rule at the end of the grace period, with the date. An assignment from any other policy is requested: review. For each group, a dynamic group is rule-managed, a group a held package grants is package-managed, and anything else is outside packages: review. The review items go to residual-review.csv for the manager of record; summary.json holds the transfer-to-review interval (PS-5's metric) once the review closes, which Chapter 07 reads. RV-02 when the review runs past ten days.`,
