      say: `The verified facts, each read on November first. The automatic policy is generally available, with the limits we've seen. Member-of rules are quarantined from November third. The create call is in version one point oh, available in the L4 and L5 clouds. And dynamic administrative units aren't available in Azure Government. Two places where Learn stops are recorded so a later edit doesn't loosen the code: the fallback approver is required, not optional, and overlap is found only among the users the population holds.`,
      detail: `Automatic assignment policy: rule on user attributes; assignments created and removed; grace period; one per package unless scopes never overlap; hidden dynamic group per policy; at most 15,000 identities; Identity Governance Administrator, not catalog owners or access package managers; GA. memberOf in a policy rule: quarantined from November 3, 2026: no assignments added or removed until removed; read-only script. Create assignmentPolicies: POST /identityGovernance/entitlementManagement/assignmentPolicies; EntitlementManagement.ReadWrite.All; example 3 with attributeRuleMembers and automaticRequestSettings; L4 and L5; v1.0. accessPackageAutomaticRequestSettings: three properties, v1.0. requestorManager: the requester's manager as approver, managerLevel 1 or 2; include another approver; v1.0. List assignments and policies: EntitlementManagement.Read.All (application, across catalogs). A user's memberships, direct and transitive: User.Read.All, L4 and L5. Direct memberships: Directory.Read.All. Dynamic administrative units: global Azure only, not Azure Government. Entitlement management, access reviews, PIM, dynamic groups: available in Azure Government, GA. Where Learn's pages differ or stop: the manager as approver: requestorManager is documented for approval stages, with the instruction to add another approver; the code requires the fallback rather than treating it as optional. Overlap: Learn says overlapping automatic policies on one package can lose access but gives no test for overlap. AA-02 evaluates the rules over a population, which finds overlap only among the users the population holds; a transition between policies over time can't be seen from one population and stays a Warn.`,
