      detail: `Step 3, lint five broken policies: python python/access_assignment.py lint tests/fixtures/ch04/bad-access --population tests/fixtures/ch04/population.json gives Policies: 5 files; Lint: 5 Finding, 2 Warn, 0 Info. AA-01 Finding: AUTO via group membership: rule uses memberOf; from November 3, 2026 the policy is quarantined and adds and removes nothing. AA-02 Finding: auto-by-department.json, auto-second-policy.json: 2 users match more than one automatic policy on one package; they can lose access. AA-05 Finding: AUTO infra admin eligibility: automatic policy doesn't both create and remove assignments. AA-07 Finding: REQUEST with no fallback: request policy doesn't route to the manager with a fallback approver. AA-09 Finding: AUTO infra admin eligibility: tier T1 access assigned by rule; privileged access is requested and activated through PIM. AA-04 Warn: AUTO Program Ops by department name: rule reads no coded slot or worker type. AA-06 Warn: grace period 30 days is over the program's 14. The exit code is 2. The two Program Operations policies overlap on the two employees of ORG-100 in the population: one rule reads the department name, the other every employee.`,
