      say: `Lab 2 uses a test tenant, never production; the authors haven't run it. Export with a read-only app, and run the member-of scan beside Learn's script: the lists must match. Create one policy from a copy of the program's file, with a one-hour grace, linted first and sent by an Identity Governance Administrator. Move a test user through the pipeline, never by hand, with the validation kit's snapshot before and after. Run the residual, give the sheet to the test manager, and measure the interval. Then back everything out.`,
      detail: `Not run by the authors. Use a test tenant in the worldwide or GCC cloud with Microsoft Entra ID Governance trial or test licenses, never production, two test access packages and three test users with coded attributes. 1 Export: register a reader app with a certificate, grant EntitlementManagement.Read.All and User.Read.All with admin consent, put a token in HRLC_GRAPH_TOKEN, run graph_export.py --task access-read --cloud gcc --param userId=<test-user-id> --out exports/access and memberof-scan; run Learn's read-only script beside it; the two lists must match. 2 Create one policy: write a copy of auto-program-operations.json pointed at your test package, with a grace period of PT1H for the test; lint the copy; write its body without _program; send it as an Identity Governance Administrator with New-MgEntitlementManagementAssignmentPolicy in PowerShell 7 (Connect-MgGraph -Scopes EntitlementManagement.ReadWrite.All). Wait several minutes, as Learn says, and confirm the matching test users receive assignments. 3 Move a test user: take the validation kit's VK-DG-05 snapshot first; change the user's organization code through the pipeline (never by hand: Chapter 01), wait for the grace period, confirm the old assignment is removed and the new one created; run VK-DG-05 against the snapshot. 4 Run the residual: export again and run residual; give the sheet to the test manager; record reviewCompletedDateTime in the mover file and run it again for the interval. 5 Back it out: Remove-MgEntitlementManagementAssignmentPolicy, choosing in the portal whether its assignments are removed, as the guide's rollback says; restore the test user's code through the pipeline; remove the reader app, its permissions and certificate; delete exports and out/ch04, with the lab's policy copy and kit runs.`,
