      say: `Here's what done looks like. Every policy in the tenant has a reviewed file, and the lint is clean over a current population. The member-of scan and Learn's script both come back empty. Each package has one automatic policy, or two whose disjointness is recorded. No privileged package is assigned by rule, and every request has a fallback approver. Every move has a residual sheet, a decision for each item, and an interval within the threshold. Next, Chapter 5 covers certificate-based authentication checks. Thanks for watching.`,
      detail: `Checklist: every assignment policy in the tenant has a file in config/access, and the lint is clean over a current population export. memberof-scan and Learn's script both return no policies. Each package has one automatic policy, or two whose disjointness is recorded and reviewed. No tier T0, T1 or privileged package has an automatic policy. Every request policy routes to the manager with a fallback approver. Every move in the period has a residual sheet, a decision for each item and a transfer-to-review interval within the threshold. The reader app holds only EntitlementManagement.Read.All and User.Read.All. In GCC High, the interim path for administrative units (a scheduled job, compared in Gate 7) is in place. Next: Chapter 05 — Certificate-Based Authentication Checks.`,
